  The CLINICAL CONTENT it encodes - the six screening items and the >= 2
  cutoff of the Short Screen for Child Sex Trafficking (SSCST) - is NOT.
  Source: Greenbaum VJ, Dodd M, McCracken C, Pediatric Emergency Care,
  PMID 26599463. That paper is not open access.

  THE REDISTRIBUTION TERMS OF THIS INSTRUMENT HAVE NOT BEEN ESTABLISHED.
  Project Harper has not obtained, and does not claim, any license to it.
  Assume permission is required before clinical or commercial use, and obtain
  your own determination from the rights holder.

  Whether encoding these items in DMN is a permitted reproduction or a
  derivative work has not been reviewed by counsel. See NOTICE at the
  repository root. Unresolved and under review.
-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/"
             xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/"
             xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/"
             xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DI/"
             id="Definitions_Greenbaum" name="GreenbaumScreen"
             namespace="http://harper.health/dmn/greenbaum">

  <!-- ALL inputs below are REQUIRED. Kogito raises a DMN error (HTTP 500) for an input that is
       absent from the request context, so callers must send every field on every call. -->

  <inputData id="ID_brokenbones" name="historyOfBrokenBonesOrCuts">
    <description>Subquestion 1a: history of broken bones or cuts needing stitches? Scored by atRiskOriginalScreen only; the modified tool (atRisk) ignores it. REQUIRED -- send it even under the modified tool.</description>
    <variable id="var_brokenbones" name="historyOfBrokenBonesOrCuts" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_knockedout" name="historyOfKnockedUnconscious">
    <description>Subquestion 1b: history of being knocked unconscious (&quot;knocked out&quot;)? Scored by both variants.</description>
    <variable id="var_knockedout" name="historyOfKnockedUnconscious" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_runaway" name="historyOfRunningAway">
    <description>History of running away from home?</description>
    <variable id="var_runaway" name="historyOfRunningAway" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_alcohol" name="historyOfAlcoholOrDrugAbuse">
    <description>History of alcohol or drug abuse (past year)?</description>
    <variable id="var_alcohol" name="historyOfAlcoholOrDrugAbuse" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_law" name="everInvolvedWithLawEnforcement">
    <description>Ever involved with law enforcement?</description>
    <variable id="var_law" name="everInvolvedWithLawEnforcement" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_std" name="historyOfSTD">
    <description>History of sexually transmitted disease?</description>
    <variable id="var_std" name="historyOfSTD" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_partners" name="numberOfSexualPartners">
    <description>Number of sexual partners; a positive item when greater than five.</description>
    <variable id="var_partners" name="numberOfSexualPartners" typeRef="number" />
  </inputData>

  <decision id="Decision_Greenbaum" name="atRisk">
    <description>Screening Tool of Greenbaum -- MODIFIED tool (Harper default). Short Screen for Child Sex Trafficking (SSCST). Positive when two or more of the six items are positive; the partner item counts positive when the number of partners exceeds five. Significant trauma is scored on subquestion 1b (knocked unconscious) alone; subquestion 1a (broken bones / cuts needing stitches) is collected but not scored. This is the modified tool reported in Table 5 of the multi-site evaluation. PERFORMANCE AT CUTOFF &gt;= 2 (Greenbaum VJ et al., J Adolesc Health 2018; n=810 across 16 sites) -- emergency department: sensitivity 83.3%, specificity 59.5%, PPV 23.8%, NPV 95.9%; total sample: sensitivity 84.4%, specificity 64.6%, PPV 23.0%, NPV 97.1%. Dropping 1a buys about 10 points of ED specificity at no cost to sensitivity, which is why Harper scores this decision by default. Even so, specificity near 60% means roughly 40% of non-victims screen positive: expect a high false-positive rate and staff the downstream referral path accordingly.</description>
    <variable id="var_atRisk" name="atRisk" typeRef="boolean" />
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRisk_1"><requiredInput href="#ID_brokenbones" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRisk_2"><requiredInput href="#ID_knockedout" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRisk_3"><requiredInput href="#ID_runaway" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRisk_4"><requiredInput href="#ID_alcohol" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRisk_5"><requiredInput href="#ID_law" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRisk_6"><requiredInput href="#ID_std" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRisk_7"><requiredInput href="#ID_partners" /></informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="le_greenbaum_modified">
      <text>(
  (if historyOfKnockedUnconscious = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfRunningAway = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfAlcoholOrDrugAbuse = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if everInvolvedWithLawEnforcement = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfSTD = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if (numberOfSexualPartners != null) and (numberOfSexualPartners > 5) then 1 else 0)
) >= 2</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>

  <decision id="Decision_GreenbaumOriginal" name="atRiskOriginalScreen">
    <description>Screening Tool of Greenbaum -- ORIGINAL screen, provided for comparison. Scores significant trauma as one item answered by two subquestions: a yes to 1a (broken bones / cuts needing stitches) OR 1b (knocked unconscious) counts once. Harper does not act on this output; the process binds atRisk. PERFORMANCE AT CUTOFF &gt;= 2 (same study) -- emergency department: sensitivity 83.3%, specificity 49.4%, PPV 20.0%, NPV 95.1%; total sample: sensitivity 84.4%, specificity 57.5%, PPV 19.9%, NPV 96.7%. The original single-site study (Greenbaum VJ, Dodd M, McCracken C, Pediatric Emergency Care, PMID 26599463) reported sensitivity 92.3%, specificity 74.4% -- better than either multi-site result; do not quote it as Harper's expected performance.</description>
    <variable id="var_atRiskOriginalScreen" name="atRiskOriginalScreen" typeRef="boolean" />
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_1"><requiredInput href="#ID_brokenbones" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_2"><requiredInput href="#ID_knockedout" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_3"><requiredInput href="#ID_runaway" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_4"><requiredInput href="#ID_alcohol" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_5"><requiredInput href="#ID_law" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_6"><requiredInput href="#ID_std" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_7"><requiredInput href="#ID_partners" /></informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="le_greenbaum_original">
      <text>(
  (if historyOfBrokenBonesOrCuts = true or historyOfKnockedUnconscious = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfRunningAway = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfAlcoholOrDrugAbuse = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if everInvolvedWithLawEnforcement = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfSTD = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if (numberOfSexualPartners != null) and (numberOfSexualPartners > 5) then 1 else 0)
) >= 2</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>

  <dmndi:DMNDI>
    <dmndi:DMNDiagram id="DMNDiagram_Greenbaum">
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_dec_mod" dmnElementRef="Decision_Greenbaum">
        <dc:Bounds x="420" y="60" width="220" height="80" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_dec_orig" dmnElementRef="Decision_GreenbaumOriginal">
        <dc:Bounds x="700" y="60" width="240" height="80" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_in1" dmnElementRef="ID_brokenbones">
        <dc:Bounds x="60" y="320" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_in2" dmnElementRef="ID_knockedout">
        <dc:Bounds x="250" y="320" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_in3" dmnElementRef="ID_runaway">
        <dc:Bounds x="440" y="320" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_in4" dmnElementRef="ID_alcohol">
        <dc:Bounds x="630" y="320" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_in5" dmnElementRef="ID_law">
        <dc:Bounds x="820" y="320" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_in6" dmnElementRef="ID_std">
        <dc:Bounds x="1010" y="320" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_in7" dmnElementRef="ID_partners">
        <dc:Bounds x="1200" y="320" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_mod1" dmnElementRef="ir_atRisk_1"><di:waypoint x="140" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="440" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_mod2" dmnElementRef="ir_atRisk_2"><di:waypoint x="330" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="465" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_mod3" dmnElementRef="ir_atRisk_3"><di:waypoint x="520" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="490" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_mod4" dmnElementRef="ir_atRisk_4"><di:waypoint x="710" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="515" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_mod5" dmnElementRef="ir_atRisk_5"><di:waypoint x="900" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="540" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_mod6" dmnElementRef="ir_atRisk_6"><di:waypoint x="1090" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="565" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_mod7" dmnElementRef="ir_atRisk_7"><di:waypoint x="1280" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="590" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_orig1" dmnElementRef="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_1"><di:waypoint x="140" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="720" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_orig2" dmnElementRef="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_2"><di:waypoint x="330" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="745" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_orig3" dmnElementRef="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_3"><di:waypoint x="520" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="770" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_orig4" dmnElementRef="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_4"><di:waypoint x="710" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="795" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_orig5" dmnElementRef="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_5"><di:waypoint x="900" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_orig6" dmnElementRef="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_6"><di:waypoint x="1090" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="845" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_orig7" dmnElementRef="ir_atRiskOriginalScreen_7"><di:waypoint x="1280" y="320" /><di:waypoint x="870" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
    </dmndi:DMNDiagram>
  </dmndi:DMNDI>
</definitions>
